  "summary": [
    "Three findings cover the service telemetry setup, route traces and metrics, and local application logs.",
    "Source shows six Flask task API routes, in-memory data and two application WARNING messages; no OpenTelemetry providers or instrumentation are configured.",
    "Prioritize reliable startup/export/shutdown, then route latency/error views and logs correlated with their request traces.",
    "No service-owner decision or external prerequisite blocks this source-backed plan. GenAI and Agent Observability resource work are outside this non-agent service scope.",
    "Select findings below and copy the generated $otel-instrument command to implement the chosen scope."
  ],
  "flow": "audit -> select -> instrument -> verify -> configure/dashboard -> publish",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "check": "Manifest",
      "finding": "Python >=3.11; Flask >=3.1 only; project python-flask-basic 0.1.0. No OTel declared, no lockfile or installed-runtime evidence.",
      "source": "pyproject.toml:1-11"
    },
    {
      "check": "Entry point",
      "finding": "Flask CLI auto-discovers app.py:app; project console script also targets flask:run. No app.run or production server is declared.",
      "source": "app.py:6; pyproject.toml:10-11; Makefile:7"
    },
    {
      "check": "Route source",
      "finding": "GET /health; GET /tasks; GET /tasks/<int:task_id>; POST /tasks; PATCH /tasks/<int:task_id>; DELETE /tasks/<int:task_id>. Flask also supplies implicit HEAD for GET and OPTIONS dispatch; no application handler for those methods.",
      "source": "app.py:32-80"
    },
    {
      "check": "Runtime/startup",
      "finding": "make dev runs uv sync then uv run flask run --port 8000 --reload. No Docker/CI/wrappers/toolchain pins/tests/test runner config found. Audit did not run make, sync or app code.",
      "source": "Makefile:3-10; pyproject.toml:5-11"
    },
    {
      "check": "GenAI ownership",
      "finding": "No",
      "source": "app.py:1-80; pyproject.toml:1-11"
    },
    {
      "check": "Trace provider topology",
      "finding": "no provider: no TracerProvider, registration, exporter, lazy helper or external bootstrap configured on the selected Flask entrypoint.",
      "source": "Makefile:7; app.py:1-80; .observe/evidence/python-otel-topology.json"
    },
    {
      "check": "Metric provider topology",
      "finding": "no provider: no MeterProvider, instruments, reader or exporter reachable.",
      "source": "app.py:1-80; .observe/evidence/python-otel-topology.json"
    },
    {
      "check": "Log provider topology",
      "finding": "no provider; classification not configured. Fixed WARNING calls exist, no OTel bridge/context injection. LoggerProvider/exporter/flush absent.",
      "source": "app.py:22-29,50-58; .observe/evidence/python-otel-topology.json"
    },
    {
      "check": "Resource precedence",
      "finding": "No standard OTel config, resource construction, hardcoded override or stability opt-in is checked in. Operator process environment not inspected; current effective runtime tuple is unverified.",
      "source": "app.py:1-80; Makefile:1-10"
    },
    {
      "check": "Local receiver",
      "finding": "No Studio status tool was available; no receiver endpoint/protocol in checked-in files. Availability unverified. Proposed HTTP/protobuf fallback is http://127.0.0.1:4318 with one /v1/<signal> leaf only after higher-precedence configuration discovery is exhausted; this is not a discovered running endpoint.",
      "source": "Makefile:1-10; pyproject.toml:1-11"
    },
    {
      "check": "Log sinks and final formatting",
      "finding": "No custom formatter/filter/adapter/handler is source configured. Flask default StreamHandler uses wsgi.errors/sys.stderr, timestamp/level/module/message formatter; exceptions can append text/tracebacks. Werkzeug CLI access/error logging is a separate category reachable through root bridging. Neither current OTel pipeline nor runtime sink emission was proved.",
      "source": "app.py:24,57; .observe/evidence/flask-source.txt"
    },
    {
      "check": "Shutdown ownership",
      "finding": "request_shutdown sets shutdown_requested and raises SystemExit; log_completed_shutdown atexit emits final WARNING only when flag set. CLI/reloader can affect signal ownership. No current telemetry teardown exists. Future logging flush must follow any emitted final callback record.",
      "source": "app.py:13-29; Makefile:7"
    },
    {
      "check": "Compatible package proposal",
      "finding": "Metadata inspected 2026-11-19: API/SDK/HTTP exporter 1.45.2 and Flask/logging instrumentors 0.66b2 align semantic-conventions/instrumentation constraints at 0.66b2, require Python >=3.10, and Flask instrumentor supports Flask >=1.0. Python 3.11 satisfies all inspected runtime minima and Flask 3.1.3 satisfies >=3.1. Latest mutually aligned metadata candidate selected; mixed release trains and deprecated SDK logging handler rejected. Full resolver/lock and installation are future implementation gates, not audit proof. No installed versions claimed.",
      "source": "https://pypi.org/pypi/opentelemetry-sdk/json; https://pypi.org/pypi/opentelemetry-instrumentation-flask/json; https://pypi.org/pypi/opentelemetry-instrumentation-logging/json; .observe/evidence/package-metadata-20261119.json"
    },
    {
      "check": "Official Flask instrumentation",
      "finding": "Current docs and inspected matching wheel support FlaskInstrumentor.instrument_app, method+rule span names, stable route duration and active-request instruments. Opt-in must precede import/creation; no current spans/metrics exist to migrate.",
      "source": "https://opentelemetry-python-contrib.readthedocs.io/en/latest/instrumentation/flask/flask.html; .observe/evidence/opentelemetry-instrumentation-flask-source.txt"
    },
    {
      "check": "Official logging bridge",
      "finding": "Current official logging package owns handler installation by default and accepts enable_log_auto_instrumentation control; deprecated SDK handler toggle can prevent the new handler. Proposal uses one current bridge and must explicitly honor OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=none rather than assuming instrumentation is disabled by exporter selection alone.",
      "source": "https://opentelemetry.io/docs/zero-code/python/configuration/; https://opentelemetry-python-contrib.readthedocs.io/en/latest/instrumentation/logging/logging.html; .observe/evidence/opentelemetry-instrumentation-logging-source.txt"
    },
    {
      "check": "Incident scope",
      "finding": "In-memory task CRUD API only: no database/client dependency calls, worker/queue, cadence/freshness contract, auth, owned canary, capacity policy, or deployment/release machinery. HTTP metrics can improve first-impact rate/latency/error detection; spans/logs localize individual failures. Infrastructure CPU/memory/instance and production traffic health remain deployment-operator context; no blocking external prerequisite found. /health remains existing static health behavior.",
      "source": "app.py:8-80; Makefile:1-10"
    },
    {
      "check": "Source revision",
      "finding": "No Git repository/revision available. SHA-256 snapshots captured for all three service source/config files. No prior audit or selection was present under the discovered service root.",
      "source": ".observe/evidence/source-snapshot.json"
    }
  ],
