  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "OTEL-001",
      "title": "Establish telemetry setup and reliable shutdown",
      "area": "Provider, resource and export lifecycle",
      "gap": "The Flask CLI starts app.py directly; no trace, metric or log provider, exporter, resource configuration or telemetry shutdown is reachable. The application has its own signal and atexit path, so future provider teardown must respect the final application log.",
      "impact": "Request signals cannot reach a receiver or be attributed to a service, environment or release.",
      "product_outcome": "Operators should be able to filter received telemetry by service and release and retain completed data at shutdown.",
      "required_fix": "Add one explicit app-owned native OTel bootstrap per process, loaded from the real Flask CLI entrypoint before serving. Create TracerProvider and MeterProvider with OTLP/HTTP batching/readers and a shared Resource; the dependent logs finding owns LoggerProvider and bridge. Honor standard endpoint/protocol precedence and operator resource overrides; default service.name=python-flask-basic and service.version=0.1.0, and use deployment.environment.name only when configured. Provide a repository-native named telemetry launch profile consumed by Makefile/Flask before SDK imports; normal profile includes local logs otlp settings when OTEL-003 is selected. Use the compatible proposal in the dated package receipt, resol
